<title>UK: MAM, Hays join UK's FTSE 100 index.</title>
<headline>MAM, Hays join UK's FTSE 100 index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London Stock Exchange said on Wednesday that Mercury Asset Management Plc (MAM) and distribution and services company Hays Plc will replace chemicals company Courtaulds Plc and glassmaker Pilkington Plc in the UK's FTSE 100 index of leading stocks.</p>
<p>The changes take effect on December 23.</p>
<p>The composition of the FTSE 100 and other indices including the FTSE mid-250 index is based on the mmarket capitalisation of the stocks. The FTSE Actuaries meets quarterly to consider the make-up of the indices.</p>
<p>Six companies slip into the mid-250 index - Thistle Hotels, Manchester United, PizzaExpress, Clyde Petroleum, WS Atkins and Biocompatibles International.</p>
<p>These replace Fine Art Developments, Matthew Clark, Courtaulds Textiles, Watmoughs, Renishaw and Chiroscience Group.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
